```python
class Channel(Protocol):
    def send(self, to: str, msg: str) -> None: ...

class EmailChannel:
    def send(self, to, msg): smtplib.SMTP("mail").sendmail("a@x.com", to, msg)

class NotificationSender:
    def __init__(self, channel: Channel, formatter: MessageFormatter):
        self._channel, self._formatter = channel, formatter
    def notify(self, user, event):
        self._channel.send(user.email, self._formatter.format(user, event))
```
Reading it end to end: `NotificationSender` now only orchestrates — it depends on the `Channel` abstraction (DIP), any new channel is a new class with zero edits here (OCP), and the interface is exactly one method (ISP).
